  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1217 PM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nAnother cool day is forecast on Tuesday as cloud cover persists \nthrough much of the day. The current forecast has highs in the upper \n50s to lower 60s, but temperatures may end up a few degrees cooler \nif cloud cover persists through most of the day. Some clearing is \nforecast across the eastern half of the area, but cloud cover will \nlikely persist in our western counties. \n\nA gradual warm up is then forecast through the end of the work week. \nHighs on Wednesday will be back into the 60s, highs on Thursday will \napproach 70, and highs on Friday will be in the lower 70s. Overnight \nlows will be in the 50s. Normal highs this time of the year are in \nthe upper 60s to near 70, while normal lows this time of the year \nare in the low to mid 40s. \n\nA large upper level trough/low is forecast to strengthen across the \nwestern CONUS late in the week. This feature is then forecast to \ntrack east across the Great Plains next weekend. This may bring our \nnext chance of rain, but there remains quite a bit of uncertainty on \nthe eventual track and strength of this system. For now, low (20-\n30%) rain chances were continued for late in the week.",
